Godot only checks that this file EXISTS; its contents are ignored, so this
note is safe to keep here where it will actually be read.

Why art/source/ is hidden from Godot's resource filesystem
(D-20260821-game-assets-are-files):

Godot 4 imports .blend files natively by INVOKING BLENDER. On a machine with
Blender installed — which, after this change, is every machine that authors
assets — the editor and every `--import` would launch Blender once per source
file and turn each into a scene resource.

That is pure cost here. Nothing at runtime reads a .blend: the shipping assets
are generated/models/*.glb and generated/vat/*.exr, baked by `just build-assets`
through the pinned bpy wheel, which is what enforces the triangle budgets, the
VAT column contract and D-081's byte-identical requirement. A second, parallel
import path producing scenes nothing loads would be slow, would differ from the
bake, and would put .import files in a directory of binary sources.

Note this does NOT hide the files from the staleness hash. tests/
test_art_assets.gd reaches them through DirAccess against the project
directory, which falls through to the real filesystem — verified, because a
.blend edited and not rebuilt MUST still fail the suite.
